-- title:
--   Kernel of evaluation at a is (X - C a)
-- statement:
--   Let $T$ be a commutative local ring which is complete and separated for the adic topology of its maximal ideal $\mathfrak m$ (i.e. `IsAdicComplete (maximalIdeal T) T`), let $a \in \mathfrak m$, and let $e : T[[X]] \to T$ be a ring homomorphism. Assume that $e$ computes adic evaluation at $a$: for every power series $f \in T[[X]]$, the value $e(f)$ agrees with [`FormalGroup.evalSeries f a`](def/FormalGroup_NSeries.html#L85), that is, with the sum $\mathrm{eval}_2(\mathrm{algebraMap}\ T\ T, a, f)$ formed in $T$ equipped with the $\mathfrak m$-adic uniform structure (the coefficient ring carrying the discrete one). The conclusion is an equality of ideals of $T[[X]]$: the kernel of $e$ is the principal ideal generated by $X - C(a)$, where $C(a)$ denotes the constant power series $a$. Thus the hypotheses on $e$ pin it down sufficiently to identify its kernel, and no further assumption on $f$ or on $e$ is made.
--
--   This is the power-series Weierstrass division statement underlying the identification of the local ring at the origin in the formal neighbourhood: evaluation at a point $a$ of the maximal ideal has kernel exactly $(X - a)$. It is used in the Drinfeld–Weierstrass origin-chart computations, in [`WeierstrassCurve.DrinfeldGlobal.map_ker_eq_span_X_sub_C_originParam`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.DrinfeldGlobal.map_ker_eq_span_X_sub_C_originParam) and in [`WeierstrassCurve.DrinfeldGlobal.nsmul_eq_one_iff_X_sub_C_originParam_dvd_nthSeries`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.DrinfeldGlobal.nsmul_eq_one_iff_X_sub_C_originParam_dvd_nthSeries).
